      ":question/problem": "What is the exact value of $\\sin\\left(195^\\circ\\right)$ without using a calculator?",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Write the angle as a sum or difference of special angles: $195^\\circ=45^\\circ+150^\\circ$.\n\nRecall the sum formula for sine:\n\n$$\n\\sin(x+y)=\\sin x\\cos y+\\cos x\\sin y\n$$\n\nSubstitute the signed unit-circle values, multiply, and combine:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sin\\left(195^\\circ\\right) &=\\sin\\left(45^\\circ+150^\\circ\\right) \\\\ &=\\sin\\left(45^\\circ\\right)\\cos\\left(150^\\circ\\right)+\\cos\\left(45^\\circ\\right)\\sin\\left(150^\\circ\\right) \\\\ &=\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\cdot \\left(-\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}\\right)+\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\cdot \\frac{1}{2} \\\\ &=-\\frac{\\sqrt{6}}{4}+\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{4} \\\\ &=\\frac{-\\sqrt{6}+\\sqrt{2}}{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
